This is the single most relevant spec item — it governs `buildCollapsiblePrompt`, `.flow-reply-prompt`, the `max-height: 30vh` internal scroll, expand-state persistence across re-renders, and `scrollIntoView` on expand — all the behaviors the fix must preserve.

```json
{
    "task_type": "bugfix",
    "scope": "src/se3/server/static/app.js (updateReplyBox / buildCollapsiblePrompt for the #flow-view docked reply panel's .flow-reply-prompt detail body), possibly src/se3/server/static/style.css, and tests under tests/frontend/ (DOM-stub coverage).",
    "complexity": "simple",
    "reasoning": "A targeted front-end defect: the reply context panel's expanded '消息详情' (.flow-reply-prompt) body has its scrollTop reset to 0 every time the 3s poll or ws STATUS_UPDATE triggers renderInterventions → updateReplyBox to wipe (ctx.innerHTML = '') and rebuild the DOM. The fix must preserve the detail body's scroll position across automatic re-renders without changing the refresh mechanism/frequency, and without regressing the existing flowReplyPromptExpanded persistence, first-expand scrollIntoView, no-scroll-on-collapse behavior, or existing DOM-stub tests. Scope is narrow and confined to one helper/panel plus a test update; no engine, server, or protocol changes. The behavioral contract for this exact panel is captured by a single spec requirement.",
    "selected_items": [
        {"spec": "running-flow-console", "requirement_name": "Collapsible Reply-Context Prompt Body"}
    ]
}
```

